        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="2" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 48px;&quot;&gt;UC19&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="120" x="-1310" y="-110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="3" parent="1" style="ellipse;html=1;shape=endState;fillColor=#000000;strokeColor=#ff0000;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="40" x="-20" y="0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="4" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#000000;rounded=1;" value="1. The Admin opens the &quot;Review tours&quot; page (queue)." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="220" x="-110" y="90" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="5" parent="1" style="rhombus;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;shapeInside=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#000000;rounded=1;" value="2. The system returns tours in &quot;AI Warning&quot; or &quot;Pending review&quot;: AI Warning first, then the longest-waiting tours first; each row has the name, status, the number of AI / location reasons, city · tour type and the submission time. E1, E2." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="220" width="320" x="-160" y="210" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="6" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#000000;rounded=1;" value="3. The Admin picks a tour." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="220" x="-110" y="490" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="7" parent="1" style="rhombus;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;shapeInside=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#000000;rounded=1;" value="4. The system shows the read-only record: tour information, moderation reasons (field, category, AI / location source, severity), the places (description, photos, audio, trigger zone, moderation status of each place), the route and the decision history. A1, E3." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="235" width="320" x="-160" y="610" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="8" parent="1" style="rhombus;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;shapeInside=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#000000;rounded=1;" value="5. The Admin chooses &quot;Approve&quot; and confirms &quot;Approve this tour?&quot;. A2, A3." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="115" width="320" x="-160" y="905" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="9" parent="1" style="rhombus;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;shapeInside=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#000000;rounded=1;" value="6. The system moves the tour to &quot;Public&quot; with a conditional update statement (only if the tour is still pending), writing the review history and the Admin action log in the same transaction. E4." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="190" width="320" x="-160" y="1080" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10" parent="1" style="rhombus;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;shapeInside=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#000000;rounded=1;" value="7. The system publishes the tour.approved event (and tour.published for the chatbot); Notification creates an in-app notification and sends an email to the author (UC#16). E6." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="175" width="320" x="-160" y="1330" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="11" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#000000;rounded=1;" value="8. The client shows &quot;Tour approved, the tour is now public&quot; and goes back to the queue; the tour appears in search and can be downloaded." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="105" width="220" x="-110" y="1565" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="12" parent="1" style="ellipse;html=1;shape=endState;fillColor=#000000;strokeColor=#ff0000;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="40" x="-20" y="1760" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="13" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#000000;rounded=1;" value="E1. No tours pending → &quot;No tours waiting for review&quot;." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="250" x="355" y="250" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="14" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#000000;rounded=1;" value="E2. No valid token → 401; not an Admin → 403, the client shows &quot;Only administrators can view this page&quot;." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="90" width="250" x="355" y="340" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="15" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#000000;rounded=1;" value="E3. Invalid tour ID format → 400; the tour does not exist → 404, the client shows &quot;This tour was not found&quot;." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="90" width="250" x="355" y="628" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="16" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#000000;rounded=1;" value="E5. Reject / request changes without a reason or over 1000 characters → 422 (&quot;Please enter a reason&quot; / &quot;Reason has at most 1000 characters&quot;), the error shows in the dialog." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="120" width="250" x="355" y="833" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="17" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#000000;rounded=1;" value="E4. The tour is no longer pending (another Admin decided first) → 409 &quot;The tour is no longer pending review&quot; and the record reloads." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="90" width="250" x="355" y="1075" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="18" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#000000;rounded=1;" value="E6. Sending the event fails → only logged; the decision still succeeds." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="75" width="250" x="355" y="1333" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="19" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#000000;rounded=1;" value="A1. View the content: the Admin listens to the audio, opens photos and views the route right in the record; the record is read-only, with no content edit buttons." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="120" width="220" x="-510" y="875" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="20" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#000000;rounded=1;" value="A2.1. The Admin chooses &quot;Reject&quot;, enters a reason (required, 1–1000 characters) and taps &quot;Reject tour&quot;. E5." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="90" width="220" x="-910" y="1050" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="21" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#000000;rounded=1;" value="A2.2. The system moves the tour to &quot;Rejected&quot;, stores the reason, writes the log and publishes tour.rejected; the author receives a notification and an email with the reason; the client shows &quot;Tour rejected&quot; and goes back to the queue." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="220" x="-910" y="1190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="22" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#000000;rounded=1;" value="A3.1. The Admin chooses &quot;Request changes&quot;, enters a general reason and / or notes per place (at least one field), then taps &quot;Send change request&quot;. E5." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="105" width="220" x="-1310" y="1050" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="23" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#000000;rounded=1;" value="A3.2. The system joins them into one reason (&quot;Place 2 – &lt;name&gt;: &lt;note&gt;&quot;), moves the tour to &quot;Needs changes&quot;, writes the log and publishes tour.changes_requested; the author receives &quot;Tour needs changes&quot;; the client shows &quot;Change request sent to the author&quot; and goes back to the queue." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="180" width="220" x="-1310" y="1205" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
